From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:23:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AOSCOS: certs: ignore trailing zero padding in X.509
 certificate list

On some targets (e.g. MIPS) the assembler moves a label defined
immediately before an alignment directive past the alignment padding.
This afflicts __cert_list_end in certs/system_certificates.S, so
system_certificate_list_size covers the zero padding (up to 255
bytes) after the last certificate and, at boot, the parser complains
after loading the certificates:

    Loaded X.509 cert 'Build time autogenerated kernel key: ...'
    Problem parsing in-kernel X.509 certificate list

The message is harmless but noisy, and the exact amount of padding
depends on the architecture and the certificate sizes.

Make x509_load_certificate_list() stop silently at an all-zero tail
instead of treating it as a malformed certificate.  Non-zero garbage
is still reported as before.  This fixes the symptom for all callers
(system certificate list, revocation list and any future users) and
for any assembler with similar label-moving behaviour.

This commit is authored with assistance from AI/LLM:

- Model: Kimi K3 (Moonshot AI)
- Platform: Moonshot AI (https://www.moonshot.ai/)
- Agent platform: Kimi Code CLI
  (https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-cli)
- Prompt:
  Investigate the "Problem parsing in-kernel X.509 certificate
  list" error seen on the loongson3 kernel build (dmesg log and
  the linux-kernel-7.0.13-2 package provided, kernel source tree
  matching the running kernel), find the root cause, then prepare
  three independent patches for the proposed fix options following
  the AOSC AI-tool usage and disclosure guidelines.

Assisted-by: Kimi-Code-CLI:Kimi-K3
---
 crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_loader.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_loader.c b/crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_loader.c
index 0d516c77cc26ac..122c11cb496a4e 100644
--- a/crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_loader.c
+++ b/crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_loader.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/key.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <keys/asymmetric-type.h>
 
 int x509_load_certificate_list(const u8 cert_list[],
@@ -15,6 +16,14 @@ int x509_load_certificate_list(const u8 cert_list[],
 	p = cert_list;
 	end = p + list_size;
 	while (p < end) {
+		/*
+		 * The certificate list may carry trailing zero padding, e.g.
+		 * when the assembler moved the end-of-list label past section
+		 * alignment padding; silently stop at an all-zero tail.
+		 */
+		if (!*p && !memchr_inv(p, 0, end - p))
+			break;
+
 		/* Each cert begins with an ASN.1 SEQUENCE tag and must be more
 		 * than 256 bytes in size.
 		 */
